// TEST: Curried Call Extent Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3016
// ============================================================================
// The curried spelling of diagnostics/075: `f(a)(b)`. The inner `f(a)` is
// desugared to a partial-application lambda before the call-site obligation
// seam sees it, and inside that lambda `b`'s slot used to be an open
// parameter, so the literal-extent check (BL3016) had nothing to compare and
// only the runtime guard in `f`'s body (BL8011) caught it.
//
// The call judgment instantiates `f`'s signature per call and pins the
// residual parameter to that instance (`T` taught by `a`), so the outer
// application compares `b`'s extent against 3 at compile time.
function f(a: T^1, b: T^1) = a + b
let a = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let b = [4.0, 5.0]
let out = f(a)(b)
